      "target": "../sections/sec-002-preface.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This module is part of the series The Immunological Basis for Immunization, \nwhich was initially developed in 1993 as a set of eight modules focusing on the vaccines \nincluded in the Expanded Programme on Immunization (EPI)1. In addition to a general \nimmunology module, each of the seven other modules covered one of the vaccines \nrecommended as part of the EPI programme, i.e. diphtheria, measles, pertussis, polio, \ntetanus, tuberculosis and yellow fever. These modules have become some of the most \nwidely used documents in the field of immunization.\nWith the development of the Global Immunizati",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The preface explains that the Immunological Basis for Immunization series began in 1993 with eight modules on the vaccines of the Expanded Programme on Immunization and has been widely used. It notes that the series is being updated and extended with new modules, including this one on mumps.",
